.TH PHARO 1 "" "pharo-cli 2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pharo \- command\-line manager for Pharo images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pharo
\fIcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
pharo\-cli is a command\-line manager for Pharo images. It creates images from the official templates, opens them with the right VM, and lets you list, rename, duplicate and remove them. Each image lives in its own folder with its own VM.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "config, c"
.B pharo config [<action>] [<key>] [<value>] [options]
.PP
Show and change settings.
.PP
Actions: list (the default) shows every setting and where its value comes from; get prints one value; set stores a value in the config file; unset removes it so the default applies again; reset removes every stored value, after you confirm.
.TP
.I <action>
list, get, set, unset or reset.
.TP
.I <key>
The setting, for get, set and unset.
.TP
.I <value>
The new value, for set.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Do not ask before reset.
.TP
.B \-\-json
With list: print a JSON object with each setting's value and origin (default, file or env), and config_file.
.TP
.B pharo config set imagesDir ~/Pharo/images
Keep new images in ~/Pharo/images.
.TP
.B pharo config set vmArgs \-\-logLevel=4
Pass \-\-logLevel=4 to the VM every time.
.SS "duplicate, d"
.B pharo duplicate [<image>] [<new\-name>]
.PP
Copy an image, with its VM, under a new name.
.TP
.I <image>
The image to copy. Without it, you choose one from a list.
.TP
.I <new\-name>
The name of the copy. Without it, the copy is called <image>\-1 (or \-2, \-3... when taken).
.TP
.B pharo duplicate MyImage
Copy MyImage as MyImage\-1.
.SS "help, h"
.B pharo help [<command>]
.PP
Show the help, for every command or for one.
.TP
.I <command>
The command to explain.
.SS "import, im"
.B pharo import <source> [<name>] [options]
.PP
Add an existing image from a folder, a zip file or a URL.
.PP
A folder is copied, not moved. The image keeps its file names. When the image has no VM and has a pharo.version file, its VM is downloaded.
.TP
.I <source>
A folder or .zip file containing a .image file, or the http(s) URL of such a zip.
.TP
.I <name>
The name of the image. Without it, the folder or zip name is used.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Print nothing but errors and warnings.
.TP
.B pharo import ~/Documents/Pharo/images/Moose
Copy an image from Pharo Launcher's images folder.
.TP
.B pharo import ~/Downloads/moose.zip Moose
Add the image in moose.zip, named Moose.
.TP
.B pharo import https://example.org/image.zip
Download a zip and add its image.
.SS "info, i"
.B pharo info [<image>] [options]
.PP
Show details about an image.
.TP
.I <image>
The image. Without it, you choose one from a list.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the details as a JSON object: name, folder, image_file, pharo_version, image_format, vm_path, template, template_url, created, last_opened (ISO 8601, UTC) and size_bytes. Unknown values are null.
.TP
.B pharo info MyImage \-\-json
Print the details of MyImage for a program.
.SS "list, l, ls"
.B pharo list [options]
.PP
List the images, most recently opened or created first.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Print only the image names, one per line.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a JSON array with one object per image, with the fields of 'pharo info \-\-json' except size_bytes.
.TP
.B pharo list \-q
Print only the names, for scripts.
.SS "new, n"
.B pharo new [<template>] [<name>] [options]
.PP
Create an image from a template.
.PP
The template is stable (the current Pharo release), latest (the newest Pharo version), a Pharo version such as 14 (its newest build), or a template id from 'pharo templates'. Without a template, the defaultTemplate setting is used.
.PP
With one argument, it is read as a template when it is a version, stable, latest or a template id, and as an image name otherwise. Use \-\-template or \-\-name when a name looks like a template.
.PP
Without a name, the image is called Pharo<version>\-<date and time>. The VM for the image is downloaded with it.
.TP
.I <template>
The template to create the image from.
.TP
.I <name>
The name of the new image.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-template <template>
The template to create the image from.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-name <name>
The name of the new image.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open the image once it is created (the default, see the autoOpenOnNew setting).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Do not open the image once it is created.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Download the template and the VM again, even when the cached copies are up to date.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Print nothing but errors and warnings.
.TP
.B pharo new
Create an image from the stable Pharo release, with a generated name.
.TP
.B pharo new 14 MyImage
Create MyImage from the newest Pharo 14 build.
.TP
.B pharo new latest \-\-no\-open
Create an image from the newest Pharo version, without opening it.
.TP
.B pharo new \-\-name 14 \-\-template stable
Name an image 14: with the flags, 14 is not read as a version.
.SS "open, o"
.B pharo open [<image>] [options]
.PP
Open an image with its VM.
.PP
The VM runs in this terminal unless \-\-background is given or the openMode setting is background. An image without a VM gets one downloaded first.
.PP
In the background, the VM's process id is printed on stdout.
.TP
.I <image>
The image to open. Without it, you choose one from a list.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-background
Run the VM in the background; its output goes to <image>/pharo\-cli.log.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-foreground
Run the VM in this terminal (the default, see the openMode setting).
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run the image without its UI, for example a server started by the image.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Print nothing but errors, warnings and the process id.
.TP
.B \-\-vm\-arg <arg>
Pass one argument to the VM. Repeat it to pass several.
.TP
.B pharo open
Choose an image from a list and open it.
.TP
.B pharo open MyImage \-\-background
Open MyImage and get the terminal back.
.TP
.B pharo open MyImage \-\-vm\-arg \-\-logLevel=4
Pass an argument to the VM.
.TP
.B pharo open MyServer \-\-headless \-\-background
Start an image without its UI and get the terminal back.
.SS "path, p"
.B pharo path [<image>] [options]
.PP
Print the folder of an image, or the images folder.
.TP
.I <image>
The image. Without it, the folder that holds all images is printed.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a JSON object with the folder as path.
.TP
.B cd "$(pharo path MyImage)"
Go to the folder of MyImage.
.SS "remove, rm"
.B pharo remove [<image>] [options]
.PP
Move an image to the trash.
.PP
When the system has no trash (Linux without gio or trash\-cli), the image is deleted for good, after you confirm.
.TP
.I <image>
The image to remove. Without it, you choose one from a list.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Do not ask before deleting for good.
.SS "rename, re"
.B pharo rename [<image>] [<new\-name>]
.PP
Rename an image.
.PP
The image folder is renamed, and so are its .image and .changes files when they carry the old name.
.TP
.I <image>
The image to rename. Without it, you choose one from a list.
.TP
.I <new\-name>
The new name. Without it, you are asked for one.
.SS "run, r"
.B pharo run [<image>] [<script>] [options]
.PP
Run a script or an expression in an image, without its UI.
.PP
The VM runs headless in this terminal and its exit status is passed on. The image is not saved unless \-\-save is given.
.PP
With \-\-temporary, a fresh image is created from a template for this run only, and removed when the run ends, however it ends.
.TP
.I <image>
The image to run. Not given with \-\-temporary.
.TP
.I <script>
A .st file to run. It is given to the image's st command\-line handler.
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-eval <expression>
Evaluate an expression and print its result, instead of running a script.
.TP
.B \-\-save
Save the image after the script or expression has run.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout <seconds>
Stop the VM after this many seconds and exit with status 124.
.TP
.B \-\-temporary <template>
Run in a fresh image made from this template, removed afterwards.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Download the template and the VM again, even when the cached copies are up to date.
.TP
.B \-\-vm\-arg <arg>
Pass one argument to the VM. Repeat it to pass several.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Print nothing but errors, warnings and what the image prints.
.TP
.B pharo run MyImage \-\-eval '3 + 4'
Print 7.
.TP
.B pharo run MyImage build.st
Run the script build.st in MyImage, then quit.
.TP
.B pharo run MyImage setup.st \-\-save
Run setup.st and keep what it changed in the image.
.TP
.B pharo run \-\-temporary 14 check.st \-\-timeout 300
Run check.st in a fresh Pharo 14 image, for at most 5 minutes.
.SS "self\-uninstall"
.B pharo self\-uninstall [options]
.PP
Remove pharo\-cli from this computer.
.PP
Removes the pharo\-cli folder, the pharo command and its man page, the block the installer added to your shell startup file, and the template cache. Your images and settings are kept.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Do not ask first.
.SS "self\-update, up"
.B pharo self\-update [options]
.PP
Update pharo\-cli to its newest release.
.TP
.B \-\-main
Update to the newest development version (the main branch) instead.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Print nothing but errors and warnings.
.TP
.B pharo self\-update \-\-main
Try the development version (the main branch).
.SS "templates, t"
.B pharo templates [<filter>] [options]
.PP
List the templates that 'pharo new' can use.
.PP
Besides these ids, 'pharo new' accepts stable, latest, and a Pharo version such as 14. The list comes from Pharo Launcher's template list and is cached (see the templatesUrl and templatesCacheTtl settings).
.TP
.I <filter>
Show only the templates whose id or name contains this text (case does not matter).
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Download the template list again instead of using the cached copy.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a JSON array with one object per template: id, name and url.
.TP
.B pharo templates moose
List the templates whose id or name contains moose.
.SS "version, v"
.B pharo version
.PP
Show the version of pharo\-cli.
.SH SETTINGS
Settings are changed with \fBpharo config set\fR \fIkey value\fR and stored in
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pharo\-cli/config\fR (\fI~/.config/pharo\-cli/config\fR by default).
An environment variable \fBPHARO_CLI_\fR\fIKEY\fR overrides the file, for example
\fBPHARO_CLI_IMAGES_DIR\fR for \fBimagesDir\fR.
.TP
.B imagesDir
Folder that holds one sub\-folder per image. Default: ~/Documents/PharoCliImages
.TP
.B defaultTemplate
Template used by 'pharo new' when none is given: stable, latest, a Pharo version such as 14, or a template id. Default: stable
.TP
.B vmStatus
Which VM build to download: the released one (stable) or the newest nightly build (latest). Default: stable
.TP
.B openMode
Whether 'pharo open' runs the VM in this terminal or in the background. Default: foreground
.TP
.B autoOpenOnNew
Whether 'pharo new' opens the image once it is created. Default: true
.TP
.B vmArgs
Arguments always passed to the VM, separated by spaces. Default: (empty)
.TP
.B picker
How to choose an image when none is named: fzf, a numbered menu (select), or fzf when installed (auto). Default: auto
.TP
.B templatesUrl
Template list in Pharo Launcher's sources.list format. Default: https://files.pharo.org/pharo\-launcher/sources.list
.TP
.B templatesCacheTtl
Seconds before the template list is downloaded again. Default: 86400
.TP
.B filesServer
Server for Pharo images and VMs (set it to use a mirror). Default: https://files.pharo.org
.TP
.B cacheDownloads
Whether template and VM zips are kept in ~/.cache/pharo\-cli/downloads, so that they are downloaded again only when the server has a newer one. Default: true
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pharo\-cli/config
User settings.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/pharo\-cli/sources.list
Cached template list.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/pharo\-cli/downloads/
Cached template and VM zips (see cacheDownloads). Safe to delete; self\-uninstall removes it.
.TP
.I <imagesDir>/<image>/
One folder per image, with its image files, its VM in pharo\-vm/ and pharo\-cli metadata in .pharo\-cli.
.SH EXIT STATUS
These codes are stable: scripts can rely on them.
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A command failed or was cancelled. For 'pharo run', the script or expression failed: the status is the VM's own.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was wrong, or a question needed a terminal (no image given, a confirmation without \-\-yes).
.TP
.B 3
No such image, script or import source.
.TP
.B 4
A download failed.
.TP
.B 5
The VM could not be started.
.TP
.B 124
\&'pharo run \-\-timeout' stopped the VM.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/jordanmontt/pharo-cli
